          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %p
            In view of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Curry-Howard+correspondence"} Curry-Howard correspondence
          %ul
            %li
              Morten Heine Sørensen, Pawel Urzyczyn, §9 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures on the Curry-Howard isomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 149
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.elsevier.com/books/lectures-on-the-curry-howard-isomorphism/sorensen/978-0-444-52077-7"} ISBN:9780444520777
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://disi.unitn.it/~bernardi/RSISE11/Papers/curry-howard.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax+-+semantics+duality"} syntax - semantics duality
            in first order logic is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Awodey"}> Steve Awodey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henrik+Forssell"} Henrik Forssell
              %em First-Order Logical Duality
              \.(
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1008.3145"}> arXiv:1008.3145
              )
          %p On the historical development:
          %ul
            %li
              José Ferreirós,
              %em The Road to Modern Logic - An Interpretation
              , The Bulletin of Symbolic Logic
              %strong 7
              no. 4 (2001) pp.441-484. (
              %a{:href => "https://idus.us.es/server/api/core/bitstreams/819edc9f-3254-4445-bc4f-6f7635521009/content"}> draft
              )
          %h3#ReferencesFromTypeTheory From type theory
          %p
            First order logic within
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            via
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              , section 3 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
